// Phase I benchmark for the SECOND domain: support reply drafts.
//
// Deliberately smaller than the reference domain - about twelve labelled
// examples per criterion. This set exists to prove the lifecycle ports without
// code changes, not to be tuned against, and the split warnings will say so
// every time you run it. Do not quote numbers computed over this file.
//
// The BASELINE-MISS cases are the same shapes as in the reference domain
// wearing different clothes, which is the part worth noticing: the failure
// TYPES port even though the criteria do not. A real number attached to the
// wrong noun, a claim that contradicts the record rather than adding to it,
// and a polite sentence that says nothing all appear here too.

// ===================== CRITERION: supported =====================

